      "writtenOn": "2024-08-20T23:58:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see. The thing I\u0027m worried about is if we add a new type, we don\u0027t want to forget to add it in doesAccessorSupportSocket. Could you switch that function to be the opposite logic, e.g. doesAccessorSupportSocket \u003d not UNIX_BOOTSTRAP and not TIPC. That way, new types added will be tested?\n\nYou can also subclass BinderRpc and call it \"BinderRpcAccessor\" and make this `TEST_P(BinderRpcAccessor, ...)` and then do this check in SetUp or similar, and that way you don\u0027t need this check at the beginning of each method or to copy it. Though no worries about that, I think it\u0027ll make sense if there is more to copy if there is a nice error message in the GTEST_SKIP.",
